      "parameters": {
        "width": 780,
        "height": 736,
        "content": "## Speech-to-Text API Endpoint with Palatine Speech\n\n**Who's it for:** Developers who need a drop-in HTTP transcription endpoint for other apps.\n\nExposes a webhook that accepts an audio file and returns the transcript as JSON.\n\n### How it works\n1. Webhook receives an audio file (multipart/form-data)\n2. Palatine Speech transcribes it\n3. Respond to Webhook returns the transcript\n\n### Setup\n1. Press **+** on the canvas, search `Palatine`, open the node and click **Install node**.\n2. Add credentials: Palatine Speech API.\n3. Set the folder / chat / database IDs on the trigger and destination nodes.\n4. Activate the workflow.\n\n### Customization\n- Add an auth-header check on the webhook\n- Return SRT/VTT instead of plain text\n- Store each transcript in a database\n\n**Requirements:** Palatine Speech API\n\n_Uses the community node **Palatine Speech** (`n8n-nodes-palatine-speech`). Install it from the nodes panel: press **+**, search `Palatine`, open the node and click **Install node**._"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
